tes", "role": "Cultural Influence"}, {"name": "Chicago, United States", "role": "Major Market"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Maxim", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "maxim"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3552325", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maxim_(magazine)"], "tags": ["United States", "magazine", "Americas", "Media & Publishing Houses", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Maxim contributed to the historical record of the Contemporary period. Key lasting impacts include: Shaped institutional landscape and community development. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Maxim played a crucial role in shaping the landscape of men's lifestyle media, influencing how masculinity and sexuality are portrayed, with over 2 million monthly copies at its height and spawning numerous imitators.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-06-17T10:10:48Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27681495147", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "American magazine Headquartered in United States. Founded 1995.", "newValue": "Maxim, an influential American magazine, was founded in 1995 in the United States, primarily targeting a male audience with a blend of lifestyle, entertainment, and culture. Its significance lies in its role as a barometer of contemporary masculinity and pop culture, reflecting shifting societal norms around gender roles and sexuality. The magazine quickly became known for its provocative content and eye-catching photography, featuring celebrities and models that defined the era's aesthetic. Key figures such as editor-in-chief Paul McGuinness and contributors like John Varvatos played pivotal roles in shaping its editorial direction and cultural impact, establishing Maxim as a staple in American media.

